## DESCRIPTION
## Optimization
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject('Calculus - multivariable')
## DBchapter('Differentiation of multivariable functions')
## DBsection('Optimization')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "PGML.pl", "MathObjects.pl");

TEXT(beginproblem());

BEGIN_PGML
A delivery of [`480`] cubic meters of gravel is to be made to a landfill. The trucker plans to purchase an open-top box in which to transport the gravel in numerous trips. The total cost to the trucker is the cost of the box plus [`$80`] per trip. The box must have height [`2`] meters but the trucker can choose the length and width. The cost of the box is [`$100/m^2`] for the ends, [`$50/m^2`] for the sides, and [`$200/m^2`] for the bottom. What size box should the trucker buy to minimize the total cost?

The optimal box is [________]{Real(4)} meters long and [________]{Real(2)} meters wide.
END_PGML

$showHint=0;
BEGIN_HINT
You will need to compute some limits to justify that this is the global minimum.
END_HINT

$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;

ENDDOCUMENT();